WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.460
Using high explosives in a chaotic firefight can be... difficult.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.140
(Casting)

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.180
Look whether you call it a Nitro Cell or a C4, there’s no arguing that it is one of the

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.520
best tools in a Defender’s arsenal.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.740
And while sometimes things can go horribly wrong, it's still a great way to get highlight

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.100
reel kills on unsuspecting enemies.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.080
(Casting)

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.400
Which is why this week on Top 10 we’re counting down the best nitro cell C4 plays in professional

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.660
Rainbow Six Siege.

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:49.220
It’s hard to stay calm and collected when you’re in a 1v1 clutch situation--especially

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.190
when you’re staring down matchpoint.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.980
But that’s exactly what meepeY did in our opening play.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:00.360
With excellent map knowledge and weapon usage, meepeY keeps his cool and throws a perfect

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.640
C4 to deny the plant and keep his team’s hopes alive.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:27.520
(Casting)

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.940
You probably don’t want to be killing teammates with your C4s… or yourself for that matter.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.820
But as our number 9 plays shows, sometimes things just work out and you win the round

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:39.829
anyway.

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:45.140
Here, Lunarmetal shows us that no sacrifice is too great in order to secure the W.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:02:01.600
(Casting)

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.260
Sometimes, if you see it, well then it’s already too late.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.200
Which is exactly what happened in our Number 8 play as Lipezord

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:16.980
accepted his fate, dying alongside his teammate with a well tossed Nitro Cell from

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.680
Cameraman.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:29.120
(Casting)

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.200
At number 7 is one of the most calculated nitro cells you’ll ever see.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.920
(Casting)

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.840
Okay, so… maybe it wasn’t on purpose… but Mark does show us that C4 can act as a

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:48.580
well placed trap that can catch a rushing enemy off guard.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.840
With Siege’s destructible environment, players have the freedom to get creative and our number

00:02:55.841 --> 00:03:00.120
six play has to be one of the craziest setups we’ve ever seen.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.379
Here, FaZe’s Mav tosses his nitro cell from the attic, through the south wall and down

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.660
the floor for a cheeky kill on some poor soul in classroom.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:36.640
(Casting)

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:45.040
Number 5 on the list takes place on a tied map of a tied series during a grand final.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:49.150
Fabian (Faye-bian) refused to let EG take the lead and pulled through with a clutch

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.100
nitro cell on Canadian.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.740
The Ash drops to the ground along with the defuser and with no time left on the clock,

00:03:55.740 --> 00:04:01.080
Fabian hides from the remaining player, stealing the round from EG in heartbreaking fashion.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:21.520
(Casting)

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.480
Never count BC out when he has a nitro cell in his pocket.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.700
Coming in at the number 4 spot we have EG on the verge of elimination.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:35.050
Fabian was looking to plant the defuser but found himself on the receiving end this time

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:37.860
around as BC’s nitro cell takes him out.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:05:03.920
(Casting)

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.800
Our number three play sees Rogue able to plant the defuser under the cover of Glaz and a

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:09.680
smoke grenade.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.600
With a 3v2 advantage, Rogue looked good to take the round but were not expecting the

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.640
C4 to come from nVk.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:34.240
(Casting)

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.440
At the runner up spot, we have RaFaLe, who lands four kills with a Nitro Cell from below.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:43.080
And to top it all off, he finishes the round with an ace.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:06:03.240
(Casting)

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:10.880
You’re in a 1v4, you’ve just run out of bullets, you’ve got a sliver of health,

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.540
one plastic explosive and a dream.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.760
Oh yeah, and you’re playing Kapkan.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:16.980
"EDD primed."

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:23.060
For SK’s Nyx in our #1 spot, he turned that dream into reality as he lobbed a hail mary

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:28.880
nitro cell down the hatch into the server room, ending the round with a swift bang.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:50.640
(Casting)

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.360
Well guys that’s all I got for you on Top 10 this week now  if you do wanna see more

00:06:55.400 --> 00:07:00.900
Rainbow Six Siege content, like the video, subscribe to the channel, and let me know in the comments

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.240
so we can make it happen.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.620
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

